# SM8550: power the UFS device down with the link off across system sleep
# (spm_lvl 5, the kernel default), instead of parking the link in hibernate
# (spm_lvl 3).
#
# SM8550's UFS PHY has no retention, so it loses its calibration in deep
# sleep either way. With the link parked (3) the first deep wake on the
# Retroid Pocket Nova failed its hibernate exit ("pwr ctrl cmd 0x18 failed")
# and needed link recovery. With the link off (5) the PHY is re-initialised
# on resume; that woke cleanly after 1 h and overnight on the Nova (UFS root).
# Level 3 was set earlier for an AYN Thor that failed to re-calibrate after
# long s2idle sleeps with the link off, before the UFS lane-clock fix
# (kernel patch 0531); re-test long sleeps on the Thor.
# "bind": spm_lvl exists only once the driver is attached.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="ufshcd-qcom", ATTR{spm_lvl}="5"
